224
00:15:57,340 --> 00:16:01,100
We all have the same goal.

225
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:08,140
However, each local expression of the church needs to contextualize their system, their culture, and their point of emphasis

226
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:11,360
in order to remain effective at that goal.

227
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,960
Churches die year after year after year.

228
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:15,140
They close their doors.

229
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:19,280
And I think the reason that they close their doors, it's not because they don't care about the Great Commission.

230
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:24,800
These are our brothers and sisters in Christ doing their best to keep their church doors open.

231
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:26,760
It's not because they don't care about the Great Commission.

232
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:31,800
It's because they've lost focus of the system, the culture, the point of emphasis.

233
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:33,460
They've missed something.

234
00:16:33,460 --> 00:16:34,980
They've gotten lulled to sleep.

235
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:38,340
They've gotten comfortable doing the things that they've always done.

236
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:45,980
And so I think if we're going to remain effective as a church at doing the thing that God has called us to do,

237
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:50,880
we have to be intentional with our system, with our culture, with our point of emphasis year in and year out.

238
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,000
We can't get lulled to sleep.

239
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:52,720
We can't get bored.

240
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:57,280
We can't get comfortable just with being here in this space with the people we're comfortable with.

241
00:16:57,280 --> 00:17:02,200
Paul says, I became all things to all people that I might reach some.

242
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:04,580
This is a very biblical principle.

243
00:17:04,580 --> 00:17:11,380
If you have ever spent any time with missionaries, effective missionaries move into the place that they're trying to reach.

244
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:16,580
And what they do is learn the culture, meet the people, get to know how things work.

245
00:17:16,580 --> 00:17:22,820
And then they define, they build a system around the culture so that they can reach the people.

246
00:17:22,820 --> 00:17:26,300
This is a very biblical principle.

247
00:17:26,300 --> 00:17:32,300
So with the rest of my time, what I want to do this morning is I want to unpack for you what I think that our system,

248
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:38,280
our culture, and I want to suggest to you what I think a point of emphasis might be for us in 2025.

249
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:39,940
It's an ambitious task.

250
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:43,640
So I'm going to have to talk really fast and you all are going to have to listen faster.

251
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:45,140
Sound good?

252
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:46,280
Okay.

253
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:47,840
Systems.

254
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:52,660
Just like in football, there are multiple systems that make up a team.

255
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:54,920
Even you sports ball people don't know that.

256
00:17:54,920 --> 00:18:01,480
I think you sports ball people, you non-sports ball people, it's hard to say.

257
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:08,960
There's offense and this is where it gets really hard for you non-sports ball people.

258
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,040
Do you know the third phase?

259
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:12,620
Hey, let's go.

260
00:18:12,620 --> 00:18:12,960
All right.

261
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,820
We got offense, we got defense, we got special teams.

262
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:20,540
And each one of those have their own system that is built to do the thing they need to do.

263
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:22,060
Now, here's the thing with church.

264
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:23,200
Here's the thing with the Great Commission.

265
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:27,600
If you look at the Great Commission, the Great Commission requires two different systems.

266
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:34,600
It says, go into all the world, make disciples, baptizing them and teaching them to obey all that I have commanded you.

267
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:40,140
There is a inherently evangelistic strategy to the Great Commission.

268
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:42,300
What do we do outside of these four walls?

269
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:44,060
What are we doing when we're out in the world?

270
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:47,680
What are we doing to go out in the world and to engage the world with the gospel?

271
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:53,480
There's an external system at play in the Great Commission and there's an internal system in play.

272
00:18:53,480 --> 00:19:02,320
Every church that wants to effectively fulfill the Great Commission has to have a strategy for how to take someone who's been baptized, who has been reached with the gospel of Jesus.

273
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:07,740
Now, what are you going to do to teach them, to encourage them, to train them to be obedient to the gospel of Jesus?

274
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:12,240
It's an internal system and an external system.

275
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:14,140
These two things work hand in hand.

276
00:19:14,140 --> 00:19:19,900
And I see there's a ton of people who are super passionate about reaching people with the gospel of Jesus.

277
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:24,260
They are missionaries to their bones, but all they want to do is get somebody to convert.

278
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:25,900
And then after that, they don't have a plan.

279
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:27,320
They don't have a strategy.

280
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:28,940
It's just like, here, pray this prayer.

281
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:31,380
Please place your faith and trust in the Lord Jesus.

282
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:32,780
And we need those people.

283
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:34,400
But we all have a calling.

284
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:35,160
We all have a gift.

285
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:36,300
And those gifts work together.

286
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:43,860
And so as a church, if we're going to be an effective church, we have to have an effective outside strategy and an effective inside strategy.

287
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:44,560
Does that make sense?

288
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,260
Okay, thank you.

289
00:19:46,260 --> 00:19:47,760
Some people are, I love it.

290
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:59,440
So this is how, and this is not how, if you read books on how to write mission, vision, and core value statements, this is not how they tell you to write mission and vision statements.

291
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:07,320
But this is how, because I'm the leader of this organization and I don't always listen to books when I read them.

292
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:10,120
Actually, I always listen to books when I read them.

293
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:15,160
No, this just kind of happened.

294
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:21,020
This kind of unfolded this way, that our mission statement really is what, it is our strategy for our internal success.

295
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:30,600
If we're going to be successful as a church that trains up disciples, that encourages disciples to learn how to obey all that Jesus commanded them, that is our mission statement.

296
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:34,520
And our vision statement really is about how do we go outside of these four walls?

297
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:38,000
And how do we reach the city with the gospel of Jesus?

298
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,080
How do we reach our community with the gospel of Jesus?

299
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:45,640
So we've broken that down into kind of an internal system and an external system.

300
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:48,020
Today, we only have time to cover the internal system.

301
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:50,640
Next week, we'll get more into the external system.

302
00:20:50,640 --> 00:20:52,040
Does that make sense?

303
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:53,200
All right.

304
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:55,420
You guys are listening really fast and really good.

305
00:20:56,820 --> 00:21:06,740
Now, really quick note, an important note, and we talked about this a little bit with the football, but systems need to be built around the people in the room.

306
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:18,700
So every once in a while, coaches get fired in the NFL, and sometimes a coach will get hired, and you'll see them come in, and they already have the system in mind that has worked for them in the past.

307
00:21:19,540 --> 00:21:22,980
And what they'll do is they'll just say, here is the system that we are going to run.

308
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:24,340
If we run this system, we will win.

309
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:34,600
But what often happens is when the coach developed the system that worked, they had a certain type of player in the room, and that system worked for those players.

310
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:38,580
But then they get to another team, and they say, this system will work if we run this system.

311
00:21:38,580 --> 00:21:46,220
But there's totally different kinds of players, and they try and force these players to play the system that was not designed for them.

312
00:21:46,220 --> 00:21:47,140
Does that make sense?

313
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:55,260
So what I want you to know about our mission statement as a church is our mission statement is not my mission statement for our church.

314
00:21:55,260 --> 00:22:00,240
It wasn't like they hired me as a pastor, and they were like, come tell us what to do.

315
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:02,400
What is your vision for the church?

316
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:05,440
As a matter of fact, I've had some conversation with you guys when I first came here.

317
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:07,340
They were like, you were like, what's your vision for the church?

318
00:22:07,340 --> 00:22:08,340
And I'm like, my vision?

319
00:22:08,340 --> 00:22:12,640
You don't want my vision, because the church is not me to you.

320
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:15,080
The church is us together, okay?

321
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:20,440
So when we built our mission, our vision, and our core value statement, I didn't build it in a room by myself.

322
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:22,060
We built it together.

323
00:22:22,060 --> 00:22:27,040
Most of you in this room, most of you that built this are in this room with me.

324
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:30,680
Like, we sat in rooms together and played on a whiteboard.

325
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:31,540
You guys remember that?

326
00:22:31,540 --> 00:22:32,080
It was fun.

327
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:33,660
I'm looking for you guys.

328
00:22:33,660 --> 00:22:34,140
It was fun.

329
00:22:34,140 --> 00:22:35,060
We had fun, didn't we?

330
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:36,020
We had fun with the whiteboard.

331
00:22:36,020 --> 00:22:36,740
Thank you, Jeremy.

332
00:22:36,740 --> 00:22:37,180
We did.

333
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:38,020
We had a great time.

334
00:22:38,020 --> 00:22:41,520
We asked for feedback from our congregation, from our leadership.

335
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:44,900
We built a system based on who we are as people.

336
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:52,180
Because God is not calling a random, unidentified group of people to lead this church.

337
00:22:52,180 --> 00:22:54,000
He's calling us to lead this church.

338
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:57,900
So this system was built around at least who was there then.

339
00:22:57,900 --> 00:23:01,500
And so if you've come since then, hopefully you've been attracted to that because you're like us,

340
00:23:01,520 --> 00:23:03,620
and you want to do things the way that we're doing things.

341
00:23:03,620 --> 00:23:08,580
And if not, hopefully you can help us get better at the thing that God's called us to do.

342
00:23:08,580 --> 00:23:10,140
All right, so system.

343
00:23:10,140 --> 00:23:11,220
Mission statement.

344
00:23:11,220 --> 00:23:13,040
This is our internal success.

345
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:17,140
This is what success looks like for us inside the walls of the church.

346
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:18,420
Hopefully you've heard it before.

347
00:23:18,420 --> 00:23:24,360
If you haven't heard it before, that's because I am really bad at repeating myself.

348
00:23:24,360 --> 00:23:29,460
They say the best leaders repeat themselves over and over and over again.

349
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,560
I don't like doing that.

350
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:35,000
Therefore, I'm bad at leading in that way.

351
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,960
So hopefully you've heard our mission statement.

352
00:23:36,960 --> 00:23:38,280
If you haven't, it is this.

353
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:40,140
This is what internal success looks like for us.

354
00:23:40,140 --> 00:23:46,640
We, as a church, invite, we are inviting real people with real lives into a Christ-centered community.

355
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:50,060
This is what success looks like for us inside the walls of the church.

356
00:23:50,060 --> 00:23:53,660
Taking people who have accepted Jesus as their Lord and Savior and encouraging them,

357
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:57,560
teaching them, training them to obey all that Jesus has commanded them.

358
00:23:57,560 --> 00:24:03,820
As a church, we are most effective when we are inviting followers of Jesus, young and old,

359
00:24:03,820 --> 00:24:12,300
on fire and flaming out on your last straw, your last-ditch effort to give this faith thing a try.

360
00:24:12,300 --> 00:24:18,500
Been around church your whole life or ran away from church and you're just now having the confidence to come back.

361
00:24:18,700 --> 00:24:22,280
Or maybe this is the first time you've ever stepped in church in your life.

362
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:23,540
It doesn't matter where you're at.

363
00:24:23,540 --> 00:24:28,740
What we do best is when we invite you, all of you, wherever you're coming from, whatever background you have,

364
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:31,640
to live into an authentic community.

365
00:24:31,640 --> 00:24:33,520
Authentic.

366
00:24:33,520 --> 00:24:35,900
Where we are actually real people.

367
00:24:35,900 --> 00:24:38,140
We're straight with who we are.

368
00:24:38,140 --> 00:24:40,060
With where we're at.

369
00:24:40,060 --> 00:24:42,740
We're not, there's no false pretense with us.

370
00:24:42,740 --> 00:24:45,060
We're honest about where we're at.

371
00:24:45,060 --> 00:24:46,820
We're living in an authentic community.

372
00:24:46,820 --> 00:24:49,820
With doubts, with struggles, with failures, and with hang-ups.

373
00:24:51,220 --> 00:24:58,920
And in the midst of the realities of our lives together, that we're pursuing submission and obedience to Jesus as the soul,

374
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:00,520
the only leader of our life.

375
00:25:00,520 --> 00:25:02,120
Not a primary leader of our life.

376
00:25:02,120 --> 00:25:05,020
Jesus is the sole leader of our life.

377
00:25:05,020 --> 00:25:07,740
It is a Christ-centered community.

378
00:25:07,740 --> 00:25:09,620
And we are going to fail.

379
00:25:09,620 --> 00:25:12,040
We fall short all of this all of the time.

380
00:25:12,040 --> 00:25:14,620
But this is what success looks like for us.

381
00:25:14,620 --> 00:25:22,000
We are at our best when we are an invitational community, an authentic community, and a Christ-centered community.

382
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:24,540
I just realized that that kind of rhymes when I say it like that.

383
00:25:24,540 --> 00:25:26,840
It's the first time I said it out loud.

384
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:27,380
I like that.

385
00:25:27,380 --> 00:25:27,620
Okay.

386
00:25:27,620 --> 00:25:31,320
I got to go back.

387
00:25:31,320 --> 00:25:33,180
We are at our best.

388
00:25:33,180 --> 00:25:34,000
Thank you.

389
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:39,980
When we are an invitational community, an authentic community, and a Christ-centered community.

390
00:25:39,980 --> 00:25:42,620
I'm preaching, people.

391
00:25:42,620 --> 00:25:43,260
Come on.

392
00:25:44,620 --> 00:25:51,540
Which is what Saquon Barkley will not be doing today because he will be on the bench.

393
00:25:51,540 --> 00:25:51,900
All right.

394
00:25:51,900 --> 00:25:54,600
Sports ball people, I'm sorry.

395
00:25:54,600 --> 00:25:56,380
Invitational.

396
00:25:56,380 --> 00:26:02,280
Following Jesus is not intended to be done out of guilt, fear, peer pressure, or religion.

397
00:26:02,280 --> 00:26:05,740
We are not here to bully you into following Jesus.

398
00:26:05,740 --> 00:26:12,880
We do not want to peer pressure you, guilt you, fear monger you into following Jesus.

399
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:15,600
And I've been a part of churches that that was their goal.

400
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:18,080
And I promise you they did it out of a good heart.

401
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:19,520
They wanted me to follow Jesus.

402
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:25,440
But what it ended up being like is me feeling like if I don't follow Jesus, these people are going to hate me and I'm going to have nowhere to belong.

403
00:26:25,440 --> 00:26:27,700
That is not how we function as a church.

404
00:26:27,700 --> 00:26:30,880
We are here to extend an invitation to you.

405
00:26:30,940 --> 00:26:36,060
If you read through the Gospels, Jesus is never guilting, peer pressuring, or forcing people into following him.

406
00:26:36,060 --> 00:26:39,980
He is regularly laying down the invitation and saying, will you come?

407
00:26:39,980 --> 00:26:42,020
Will you follow me?

408
00:26:42,020 --> 00:26:44,780
And to follow me, it will require sacrifice.

409
00:26:44,780 --> 00:26:46,860
It will require laying down your life.

410
00:26:46,860 --> 00:26:49,080
But I'm not forcing that on you.

411
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:50,360
I'm not guilting you into that.

412
00:26:50,420 --> 00:26:54,720
I am inviting you into a relationship with me.

413
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:58,800
We want to extend invitation to the life that we found.

414
00:26:58,800 --> 00:27:05,140
Authentic, true life, genuine community can only be found when we're honest about where we are.

415
00:27:05,780 --> 00:27:11,600
You'll never experience abundant life that Jesus has to offer if you're pretending to be someone you're not.

416
00:27:11,600 --> 00:27:24,060
And I know that that is, it's easier sometimes to come in here, to put on your church shirt, to put on your church face, to go back to the coffee bar, to grab your coffee, and to just be like, you know what?

417
00:27:24,060 --> 00:27:25,620
Somebody asked me how I'm doing.

418
00:27:25,620 --> 00:27:29,080
I'm going to say good because I don't want to get into it right now.

419
00:27:30,380 --> 00:27:37,180
If we're going to be effective at doing the thing God's called us to do, we've got to lay down the pretense, and we've got to be honest with people about where we're at.

420
00:27:37,180 --> 00:27:41,920
I can't tell you how many times I've walked past conversations in the lobby where I've overheard someone say, how are you doing?

421
00:27:41,920 --> 00:27:44,540
And I've heard the person say back to them, are you sure you want to know?

422
00:27:44,540 --> 00:27:47,460
I love that about our church.

423
00:27:47,460 --> 00:27:49,980
May that continue to be true about our church.

424
00:27:49,980 --> 00:27:53,660
And I'm not saying you have to dump all of your stuff on random strangers you don't know.

425
00:27:53,660 --> 00:28:00,120
Sometimes it might take time for you to find the people that you can trust with your stuff.

426
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:04,140
But may we not pretend to be someone we aren't.

427
00:28:04,140 --> 00:28:09,240
Throughout the Gospels, especially in John, we see Jesus always inviting people into the light.

428
00:28:09,240 --> 00:28:11,180
There's freedom in the light.

429
00:28:11,180 --> 00:28:12,540
There's growth in the light.

430
00:28:12,540 --> 00:28:13,940
There's victory in the light.

431
00:28:13,940 --> 00:28:20,260
And the enemy of God wants you to slink back into the darkness because darkness is where death and destruction happens.

432
00:28:20,260 --> 00:28:30,220
Some of you have blown up your lives, and you know, you know for a fact that you never would have blown up your life if you would have just been honest about where you were 10 steps before you blew up your life.

433
00:28:30,380 --> 00:28:41,240
Some of you are in the shadows right now, dealing with all kinds of messy stuff in your life, and you're too afraid to tell somebody about it.

434
00:28:44,580 --> 00:28:49,620
If we're going to be an effective church that obeys the teachings of Jesus, we just got to be honest with where we're at.

435
00:28:49,620 --> 00:28:51,100
We are welcome at the foot of the cross.

436
00:28:51,100 --> 00:28:52,940
The Father's arms are open wide.

437
00:28:54,840 --> 00:29:03,880
And if we are a church, those of you that receive that, if you receive that with guilt or condemnation or shame, this is not the place for you.

438
00:29:03,880 --> 00:29:08,960
We receive people's confession, people's failures, people's realities of life.

439
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:11,220
We receive it with grace and with mercy.

440
00:29:11,220 --> 00:29:15,280
Lastly, it's Christ-centered.

441
00:29:15,280 --> 00:29:24,080
Our church's primary identity is not rooted in a specific theological set of convictions, but rather it's focused on obedience to the life and teachings of Jesus.

442
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:26,760
You can have your theological convictions here.

443
00:29:26,760 --> 00:29:29,480
You can believe things deeply.

444
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:36,360
We should wrestle with theology, but at the end of the day, as a church, we don't define ourselves based on our theological convictions.

445
00:29:36,360 --> 00:29:48,600
We define ourselves based on children of the living God, submitted to the lordship of Jesus, and doing whatever we can to obey the teachings that he gave us, which are primarily love God with all your heart, soul, mind, and strength, and love your neighbor as yourself.

446
00:29:48,600 --> 00:29:51,780
And you don't have to have a great systematic theology to do that well.

447
00:29:51,780 --> 00:29:59,760
The mission statement of our church is rooted in Scripture.

448
00:29:59,760 --> 00:30:03,000
It's bathed in prayer, and it's born out of a community of believers.

449
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:05,060
We made this together, some of you in this room.

450
00:30:06,360 --> 00:30:13,520
But this is a sermon, and since I haven't read the Bible yet, you guys should be questioning when that's coming.

451
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:15,420
Thank you.

452
00:30:15,420 --> 00:30:19,340
I don't want you to think I'm making this stuff up, so let's read from Hebrews.

453
00:30:19,340 --> 00:30:24,580
I think this verse really does a good job of summarizing our mission statement as a church.

454
00:30:24,580 --> 00:30:31,480
By his death, Jesus opened up a new and life-giving way through the curtain of the most holy place.

455
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:40,620
And since we have a great high priest who rules over God's house, let us go right into the presence of God with sincere hearts, fully trusting in him.

456
00:30:40,620 --> 00:30:46,620
The gospel of Jesus has opened up this free access to God, the Father, through the blood of Jesus.

457
00:30:46,620 --> 00:30:48,440
We are welcome as we are.

458
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:52,360
We should come as we are into the presence of God, fully trusting in him.

459
00:30:52,360 --> 00:30:58,480
For our guilty conscience had been sprinkled with Christ's blood to make us clean, and our bodies had been washed with pure water.

460
00:30:58,480 --> 00:31:03,480
Therefore, let us hold tightly without wavering to the hope that we affirm.

461
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:09,880
If this is the hope that we affirm, if our life is built on being accepted to the creator God of the universe through the blood of Jesus,

462
00:31:09,880 --> 00:31:12,420
we should build our entire lives around that.

463
00:31:12,420 --> 00:31:13,620
We should hold tightly to that.

464
00:31:13,620 --> 00:31:15,360
We should let nothing take that away from us.

465
00:31:16,360 --> 00:31:18,380
For God can be trusted to keep his promises.

466
00:31:18,380 --> 00:31:22,600
Let us think of ways to motivate one another to acts of love and good works,

467
00:31:22,600 --> 00:31:25,580
and let us not neglect our meeting together, as some people do,

468
00:31:25,580 --> 00:31:31,160
but encourage one another, especially now that the days are drawing near.

469
00:31:33,060 --> 00:31:39,400
We are a people who are inviting people into authentic community, focused on obedience to Jesus,

470
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:44,360
which leads us to our culture, and I have to go fast, so you'll have to listen even faster.

471
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:51,960
I love the importance that the writer of Hebrews puts on the individual believers to encourage one another to obedience.

472
00:31:51,960 --> 00:31:59,320
The reality is we could have paid the best marketing team in the area to write us the catchiest mission statement,

473
00:31:59,320 --> 00:32:00,760
vision statement of all time.

474
00:32:01,500 --> 00:32:07,240
We could spend thousands of dollars plastering it all over our building on billboards.

475
00:32:07,240 --> 00:32:11,320
We could have gotten it all out there, but the reality is it doesn't matter what we put on paper.

476
00:32:11,320 --> 00:32:17,580
If you all and us and me, if we as leaders and those of you in the chairs of the church,

477
00:32:17,580 --> 00:32:20,860
serving in the church, taking the mission of the gospel outside of these walls,

478
00:32:20,860 --> 00:32:24,940
if you all don't live into what we've said we're about,

479
00:32:24,940 --> 00:32:27,540
then it doesn't matter what we have on paper.

480
00:32:29,940 --> 00:32:35,320
The culture is built by each individual believer doing the thing that God is calling us to do.

481
00:32:37,460 --> 00:32:46,540
We have four core, what most organizations call core values, but again, the lovely pastor Matt Lewis, who many of us love so very much,

482
00:32:46,540 --> 00:32:48,500
would not let us call it core values.

483
00:32:48,500 --> 00:32:54,220
He wanted to call it core practices because he said core values don't mean anything, again, if you don't do something about it.

484
00:32:54,220 --> 00:32:58,500
So these things are things that we are called to do as individual believers.

485
00:32:58,660 --> 00:33:01,340
Each one of these probably requires a sermon in and of itself.

486
00:33:01,340 --> 00:33:06,180
Hopefully we'll do that soon, but for now, I'm just going to run through them, give you the elevator pitch.

487
00:33:06,180 --> 00:33:12,180
And as I work through these, I'd love for you to consider, are these values that you are actively and intentionally embodying?

488
00:33:12,180 --> 00:33:17,060
And if not, what things can you do to begin to embody these?

489
00:33:17,060 --> 00:33:19,760
Because what you embody is our culture.

490
00:33:19,920 --> 00:33:21,460
Again, it doesn't matter what I put on paper.

491
00:33:21,460 --> 00:33:26,300
What we do as a community of believers is our culture.

492
00:33:26,300 --> 00:33:29,580
So this is what we want our culture to be.

493
00:33:29,580 --> 00:33:31,240
Are we living this way?

494
00:33:31,240 --> 00:33:35,500
First, I won't belabor this point because we talked about it in our mission statement,

495
00:33:35,500 --> 00:33:42,080
but our first cultural practice, core practice, is that we prioritize real relationships.

496
00:33:42,080 --> 00:33:44,320
Real, emphasis on real.

497
00:33:44,320 --> 00:33:46,660
Church isn't a place where we go to worship on Sundays.

498
00:33:46,660 --> 00:33:48,560
It is a family that we belong to.

499
00:33:48,560 --> 00:33:52,660
We should not rush in and out of this place.

500
00:33:52,660 --> 00:33:59,060
We should not just attend when it's convenient for us.

501
00:33:59,060 --> 00:34:02,660
We shouldn't only see each other on Sundays.

502
00:34:03,380 --> 00:34:08,840
We should be in each other's living rooms, at our kids' extracurricular activities.

503
00:34:08,840 --> 00:34:12,840
We should be the ones we call when life kicks us in the teeth.

504
00:34:12,840 --> 00:34:16,980
We prioritize real relationships.

505
00:34:16,980 --> 00:34:17,720
And here's the deal.

506
00:34:17,720 --> 00:34:21,480
In a room this big, sometimes it can be hard to find that.

507
00:34:21,480 --> 00:34:24,740
If you're new here, you might be realizing, you might be seeing,

508
00:34:24,740 --> 00:34:27,720
wow, there's a lot of circles of people that are happening in this building,

509
00:34:27,720 --> 00:34:29,780
and it seems like people have these relationships.

510
00:34:29,780 --> 00:34:32,480
They're in each other's lives, but I can't find it.

511
00:34:33,700 --> 00:34:36,320
That's on us, partially, and it's also on you.

512
00:34:36,320 --> 00:34:37,900
We've got to work together.

513
00:34:37,900 --> 00:34:41,680
This takes time for you to build relationships of trust.

514
00:34:41,680 --> 00:34:46,880
And if you're new here, just know that we want you to find that community here.

515
00:34:46,880 --> 00:34:49,460
We want you to find a place where you can belong, where you can be real,

516
00:34:49,460 --> 00:34:54,420
where you can be honest, where you have somebody to call when life kicks you in the teeth.

517
00:34:55,620 --> 00:34:57,660
Second, we unite for the sake of the gospel.

518
00:34:57,660 --> 00:35:04,360
This is one that I am super passionate about, and lucky for us, Jesus is passionate about it too.

519
00:35:04,360 --> 00:35:08,920
John 17, the final prayer that he prays before going to the cross,

520
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:13,720
he prays that the church would be one as he and the Father are one.

521
00:35:13,720 --> 00:35:19,880
The stakes of the gospel are too high for us to fight and divide over secondary theology.

522
00:35:21,880 --> 00:35:25,700
Far too many churches split over issues that are complex and difficult,

523
00:35:25,700 --> 00:35:31,180
and that the smartest biblical scholars on earth today could spend hours and hours debating over

524
00:35:31,180 --> 00:35:32,620
and never come to the right conclusion.

525
00:35:32,620 --> 00:35:33,240
Why?

526
00:35:33,240 --> 00:35:36,700
Why on earth would we split and go to a church down the road

527
00:35:36,700 --> 00:35:41,540
because we disagree with something complex that we're both probably wrong on at the end of the day?

528
00:35:42,660 --> 00:35:46,420
The amount of times I've seen people walk out of churches because they're like,

529
00:35:46,420 --> 00:35:50,720
oh, they believe this and I believe this, and I'm like, you're probably both wrong.

530
00:35:50,720 --> 00:35:55,520
The gospel has to be the primary thing that we focus on.

531
00:35:55,520 --> 00:35:58,700
Obedience to Jesus, it has to be our focus.

532
00:35:58,700 --> 00:36:03,840
We should talk about, wrestle through theological disagreements and interpretations of the text.

533
00:36:03,840 --> 00:36:04,820
It makes us better.

534
00:36:04,820 --> 00:36:06,480
It gets us closer to the truth.

535
00:36:07,340 --> 00:36:13,140
But if they aren't crucial to the message of the gospel, we should learn to live in unity with one another.

536
00:36:13,140 --> 00:36:16,200
Make sense?

537
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:17,540
All right.

538
00:36:17,540 --> 00:36:20,760
Third, we rely on the written and living word of God.

539
00:36:20,760 --> 00:36:25,000
At Canvas Community Church, we long to be a people of the word.

540
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:28,500
We believe the Bible is inspired by God.

541
00:36:28,500 --> 00:36:40,700
And it contained within this from Genesis to Revelation is a unified and redemptive story.

542
00:36:40,700 --> 00:36:43,180
Watch my back, all right?

543
00:36:43,180 --> 00:36:49,220
Why are you guys laughing?

544
00:36:49,220 --> 00:36:50,620
Oh, Scott's got it.

545
00:36:50,620 --> 00:36:50,920
All right.

546
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:52,920
Don't mess with Scott.

547
00:36:52,920 --> 00:36:55,360
We are a people of the word.

548
00:36:55,420 --> 00:36:56,960
We believe the Bible is inspired by God.

549
00:36:56,960 --> 00:36:59,700
It is a unified and redemptive story that points to Jesus.

550
00:36:59,700 --> 00:37:03,000
This is why we say we rely on not just the written word, but the living word.

551
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:07,540
John 1 says that Jesus is the word became flesh, dwelt among us.

552
00:37:07,540 --> 00:37:16,900
This Bible all points to Jesus, who is the ultimate fulfillment and ultimate revelation of who God is and what he's like.

553
00:37:18,480 --> 00:37:25,760
Every decision we make and belief we have should be rooted in the Scriptures and the life teaching, life and teachings of Jesus.

554
00:37:25,760 --> 00:37:28,640
It's a lifelong process of learning and surrender.

555
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:30,080
Here's what I would say.

556
00:37:30,080 --> 00:37:42,100
If your ideas about God have not changed over a year, two years, five years, ten years of interacting with the Scriptures and community with other believers.

557
00:37:42,900 --> 00:37:51,620
If you, like, if your Bible teacher, ten years ago taught you what this verse means and you're just like, he told me that's what it means and that's what it means and I don't care what else.

558
00:37:52,620 --> 00:37:55,400
You are, you are, you are, you are in danger.

559
00:37:55,400 --> 00:38:02,840
Constantly evaluate your beliefs and your lifestyle on the Scripture of Jesus.

560
00:38:02,840 --> 00:38:21,040
If you just embrace a teaching that somebody gave you and you don't think through it and you don't work through it in community with others, you will get stuck in a rut of fundamental religious theology and the Holy Spirit won't have any room to, to mold you and to make you into the person he's inviting you to be.

561
00:38:22,040 --> 00:38:24,780
This book is a two-edged sword.

562
00:38:24,780 --> 00:38:29,660
It's a lifelong process of learning.

563
00:38:29,660 --> 00:38:33,180
He's inviting us to be challenged by the Scriptures.

564
00:38:33,180 --> 00:38:38,000
Fourthly, we, lastly, we cultivate our spiritual gifts to serve others.

565
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:43,820
Each and every person who has submitted their life to Jesus has been given a spiritual gift.

566
00:38:43,820 --> 00:38:46,680
We've been called to serve together in community.

567
00:38:46,680 --> 00:38:48,520
The church is not a spectator sport.

568
00:38:48,520 --> 00:38:51,840
There aren't star players and bench players.

569
00:38:52,040 --> 00:38:56,680
We all have a unique role to play.

570
00:38:56,680 --> 00:38:59,660
And if we opt out, the whole church misses out.

571
00:39:02,860 --> 00:39:04,340
Okay, non-sportsball people.

572
00:39:04,340 --> 00:39:06,120
I'm gonna give one more sportsball illustration.

573
00:39:06,120 --> 00:39:06,540
You okay?

574
00:39:06,540 --> 00:39:17,100
Today is probably the most boring week in NFL football because most of the playoffs have already been decided.

575
00:39:17,100 --> 00:39:24,080
So there's a ton of games that mean absolutely nothing for anyone except for the people that are trying to get bonus money for whatever reason.

576
00:39:25,540 --> 00:39:31,920
And there has been talk all this week about which of the star players are gonna sit on the bench so they don't get hurt before the playoff.

577
00:39:32,860 --> 00:39:36,400
Because certain players in football are more important than other players.

578
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:38,820
Not so in the church.

579
00:39:38,820 --> 00:39:42,020
Not so in the church.

580
00:39:42,020 --> 00:39:44,820
I don't care what your spiritual gift is, what your calling is.

581
00:39:44,820 --> 00:39:48,940
I don't care if what you do is done in the back room when nobody sees it or knows it.

582
00:39:48,940 --> 00:39:50,020
We talked about it this morning.

583
00:39:50,140 --> 00:39:54,040
Dave Calhoun does something in the back room that most of you probably didn't even know about.

584
00:39:54,040 --> 00:39:56,220
But if he didn't do it, we would miss out.

585
00:39:56,220 --> 00:40:01,580
We all have a valuable, important part to play.

586
00:40:01,580 --> 00:40:03,400
And listen, it's okay to rest for a season.

587
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:06,160
It's okay to heal for a season.

588
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:11,340
Our church tends to be a church that people come to when they're just beaten down.

589
00:40:11,340 --> 00:40:15,040
When they've gotten broken down by the church.

590
00:40:15,500 --> 00:40:22,380
And if you need a season of rest, if you need to just process the pain that you've been through with God and you're like,

591
00:40:22,380 --> 00:40:25,540
I'm not ready to jump in and start serving or do any of that, that's okay.

592
00:40:25,540 --> 00:40:28,720
This is a place, a safe place where you can rest, where you can take a break.

593
00:40:28,720 --> 00:40:36,160
But at the end of the day, don't let that break extend too long because all of us are called to be in regular participation in the church.

594
00:40:36,160 --> 00:40:38,760
It should be the goal of every follower of Jesus.

595
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:40,660
Romans 12 says this,

596
00:40:40,660 --> 00:40:44,680
In his grace, God has given us different gifts for doing certain things well.

597
00:40:45,140 --> 00:40:49,860
So if God has given you the ability to prophesy, speak with as much faith as God has given you.

598
00:40:49,860 --> 00:40:51,920
If your gift is serving others, serve them well.

599
00:40:51,920 --> 00:40:53,520
If you are a teacher, teach well.

600
00:40:53,520 --> 00:40:56,480
If your gift is to encourage others, be encouraging.

601
00:40:56,480 --> 00:40:59,300
If it is giving, give generously.

602
00:40:59,300 --> 00:41:03,460
If God has given you leadership ability, take responsibility seriously.

603
00:41:03,460 --> 00:41:05,760
Listen to podcasts and read audio books.

604
00:41:05,760 --> 00:41:06,440
I'm just kidding.

605
00:41:09,180 --> 00:41:12,920
And if you have a gift for showing kindness to others, do it gladly.

606
00:41:12,920 --> 00:41:16,360
If you've been given a gift, pour it out with gladness.

607
00:41:16,360 --> 00:41:17,460
I love this.

608
00:41:17,460 --> 00:41:18,980
Don't just pretend to love others.

609
00:41:18,980 --> 00:41:28,060
Don't do the churchy version of I'm thinking about you and praying for you and not follow up.

610
00:41:28,060 --> 00:41:29,720
Don't just pretend to love others.

611
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:30,840
Really love them.

612
00:41:30,840 --> 00:41:31,580
Hate what is wrong.

613
00:41:31,580 --> 00:41:32,820
Hold tightly to what is good.

614
00:41:32,820 --> 00:41:37,400
Love each other with a genuine affection and take delight in honoring each other.

615
00:41:37,400 --> 00:41:42,160
Never be lazy, but work hard and serve the Lord enthusiastically.

616
00:41:42,160 --> 00:41:45,140
Rejoice in our confident hope.

617
00:41:45,140 --> 00:41:47,500
Be patient in trouble and keep on praying.

618
00:41:47,500 --> 00:41:51,020
When God's people are in need, be ready to help them.

619
00:41:52,620 --> 00:41:55,940
Always be eager to practice hospitality.

620
00:41:55,940 --> 00:42:01,840
Which leads me to the last point on the outline.

621
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:02,880
Aren't you guys so thankful?

622
00:42:02,880 --> 00:42:04,100
You guys listen fast.

623
00:42:04,100 --> 00:42:05,160
We're there.

624
00:42:05,160 --> 00:42:08,260
We've made it to our point of emphasis.

625
00:42:08,260 --> 00:42:13,500
And I'm not the type of person that usually like has a word for the year.

626
00:42:13,500 --> 00:42:15,080
How many people like to do a word for the year?

627
00:42:15,080 --> 00:42:16,260
I think it's awesome.

628
00:42:16,260 --> 00:42:18,940
I would love to be able to do a word for the year.

629
00:42:18,940 --> 00:42:23,720
I just like, I'm a perfectionist when it comes to those things.

630
00:42:23,720 --> 00:42:25,060
So I'll sit and I'll get a word.

631
00:42:25,060 --> 00:42:26,280
And I'll be like, nope, that's not good enough.

632
00:42:26,280 --> 00:42:29,760
So I want like, anyway, I just can't do it.

633
00:42:29,760 --> 00:42:35,060
But this year, as I reflected on 2024 and thought and prayed and talked to the leaders of our church

634
00:42:35,060 --> 00:42:40,260
about the future of our church, I kept coming back to one major point of emphasis for our church.

635
00:42:40,260 --> 00:42:44,140
I actually had like a phrase in mind that just keeps coming back,

636
00:42:44,140 --> 00:42:46,420
keeps repeating over and over and over in my head.

637
00:42:47,420 --> 00:42:49,940
And that phrase is make room.

638
00:42:49,940 --> 00:42:53,700
Always be eager to practice hospitality.

639
00:42:53,700 --> 00:42:56,100
Make room for God and for one another.

640
00:42:56,100 --> 00:43:02,480
The world around us is increasingly busy and distracted.

641
00:43:02,480 --> 00:43:05,720
We are being pulled in a million different directions.

642
00:43:05,720 --> 00:43:09,400
I'm sure if you look at your calendar for January, the first month,

643
00:43:09,400 --> 00:43:14,020
the month that's supposed to be slow, everything's closed, snow is falling,

644
00:43:14,020 --> 00:43:16,280
your calendar's probably already filled to the brim.

645
00:43:17,420 --> 00:43:23,740
Followers of Jesus have to be intentional to make space for God to direct our lives

646
00:43:23,740 --> 00:43:27,980
so that we can be obedient to the things that he's calling us to.

647
00:43:27,980 --> 00:43:30,840
Not only that, but our city is growing.

648
00:43:30,840 --> 00:43:32,660
Our neighborhood is expanding.

649
00:43:32,660 --> 00:43:35,980
We all have people in our lives we are praying to come

650
00:43:35,980 --> 00:43:38,860
that will come to know and follow Jesus.

651
00:43:38,860 --> 00:43:43,340
This is the part that's not going to be fun for some of you, okay?

652
00:43:43,340 --> 00:43:44,700
Just warning you.

653
00:43:44,700 --> 00:43:46,440
Just give me 10 minutes, we'll be done,

654
00:43:46,440 --> 00:43:48,820
and hopefully I'll answer some of your fears, your questions.

655
00:43:50,400 --> 00:43:52,800
I don't know if you tried to find a parking spot this morning

656
00:43:52,800 --> 00:43:55,980
or check in a kid lately, but we're pretty much out of space.

657
00:43:59,120 --> 00:44:02,740
So if we're going to be a church that regularly invites people

658
00:44:02,740 --> 00:44:06,600
to find a Christ-centered community to live into,

659
00:44:06,600 --> 00:44:11,100
we've got to be intentional about making room for people.

660
00:44:11,100 --> 00:44:14,360
So this is something we're praying about as a leadership team.

661
00:44:14,360 --> 00:44:16,120
We invite your feedback.

662
00:44:16,120 --> 00:44:19,640
We're praying about the possibility of launching a second service

663
00:44:19,640 --> 00:44:21,400
on Easter Sunday this year.

664
00:44:22,800 --> 00:44:24,460
Not only do we need to make room in the building,

665
00:44:24,460 --> 00:44:27,640
this is not just about this gathering, Sunday morning gathering.

666
00:44:27,640 --> 00:44:28,980
We need to expand our small groups.

667
00:44:28,980 --> 00:44:31,840
There are people in here who want to have community,

668
00:44:31,840 --> 00:44:34,140
who want to get out of rows and into circles,

669
00:44:34,140 --> 00:44:36,180
and they can't find it because we don't have enough room,

670
00:44:36,180 --> 00:44:38,580
we don't have enough space for people in our living rooms.

671
00:44:38,580 --> 00:44:41,340
So that's something that you might be passionate about,

672
00:44:41,340 --> 00:44:42,400
you might feel called to.

673
00:44:42,400 --> 00:44:46,120
And even if you don't feel passionate or called to it,

674
00:44:46,120 --> 00:44:49,460
let me read the end of that passage again,

675
00:44:49,460 --> 00:44:52,760
because I'm not super passionate, nor do I feel called to it.

676
00:44:52,920 --> 00:44:56,120
But the Scriptures say, always be eager to practice hospitality.

677
00:44:56,120 --> 00:45:01,440
There are about 150 apartments getting put in right behind our lot.

678
00:45:01,440 --> 00:45:06,240
Do we want space for those people to find the message of Jesus,

679
00:45:06,240 --> 00:45:09,660
to be embraced into a community where they can be loved and cared for

680
00:45:09,660 --> 00:45:13,700
and taught and trained what true abundant life looks like?

681
00:45:13,700 --> 00:45:17,580
Always be eager to practice hospitality.

682
00:45:17,580 --> 00:45:21,360
Now, I realize that this probably is not exciting news for a lot of us.

683
00:45:22,000 --> 00:45:25,800
I know that there are many of us in this room who have had bad experiences with bigger churches.

684
00:45:25,800 --> 00:45:29,580
You're afraid of losing the family atmosphere that we have here.

685
00:45:29,580 --> 00:45:33,360
Did I just insert some of the thoughts?

686
00:45:33,360 --> 00:45:37,040
I've had conversations with some of you, so I'm actually quoting you back to you.

687
00:45:37,040 --> 00:45:39,880
That's the problem when you talk to the pastor.

688
00:45:39,880 --> 00:45:42,420
Sometimes he'll quote you back to you.

689
00:45:43,800 --> 00:45:44,600
I get it.

690
00:45:44,600 --> 00:45:47,600
Let me share two quick thoughts that I think will help.

691
00:45:47,600 --> 00:45:50,380
First, my heart's desire for us is not to become a big church.

692
00:45:50,380 --> 00:45:55,360
I have no desire or ambition to lead a big church if it were up to me.

693
00:45:56,640 --> 00:46:01,800
If we go to two services and I'll grow two services, I would love for us to do something like plant a church

694
00:46:01,800 --> 00:46:04,100
or partner with other churches who are struggling.

695
00:46:04,100 --> 00:46:06,960
I have no desire to raise money to build a bigger building.

696
00:46:06,960 --> 00:46:08,840
This is the building I hope to die in.

697
00:46:09,480 --> 00:46:12,580
And not because it's nice, but because it'll be paid for.

698
00:46:12,580 --> 00:46:21,080
If we're going to raise money, let's raise money to do something for people in need in our community.

699
00:46:22,280 --> 00:46:25,800
So let's make as much space as we can make in this building, and when we run out of space,

700
00:46:25,800 --> 00:46:31,540
then we'll go send some people out, and we'll do whatever we can to embody the gospel of Jesus in our community.

701
00:46:31,540 --> 00:46:33,520
So I don't want us to be big.

702
00:46:33,520 --> 00:46:34,480
That's not the goal here.

703
00:46:34,480 --> 00:46:40,040
Second, this is where I think some of you will like this.

704
00:46:40,040 --> 00:46:42,280
I'm not super excited about it either.

705
00:46:42,280 --> 00:46:48,240
I love our church as it is, and I would be content to close the doors and keep it like this forever.

706
00:46:48,240 --> 00:46:50,040
One problem.

707
00:46:50,040 --> 00:46:51,740
Any guesses?

708
00:46:53,080 --> 00:46:54,820
The Great Commission, all right?

709
00:46:54,820 --> 00:46:59,100
I can't tell you the amount of times I've been like, let's just close the doors.

710
00:46:59,100 --> 00:47:00,600
And I'm like, oh, wait.

711
00:47:00,600 --> 00:47:02,700
Go into all the world, make disciples.

712
00:47:02,700 --> 00:47:04,580
Like, that's why we exist.

713
00:47:04,580 --> 00:47:09,820
So I have personally wrestled with this possibility, this struggle for a while,

714
00:47:09,820 --> 00:47:12,540
and God keeps bringing me back to a passage in Mark chapter 6.

715
00:47:12,540 --> 00:47:17,800
We don't have time to read it, so I've summarized the Cliff Notes version in the outline.

716
00:47:17,800 --> 00:47:23,580
And the disciples have been sent out two by two to do miraculous things in the name of Jesus.

717
00:47:23,580 --> 00:47:24,260
They come back.

718
00:47:24,260 --> 00:47:26,300
They're exhausted from a hard season of ministry.

719
00:47:26,620 --> 00:47:28,120
What they want more than anything.

720
00:47:28,120 --> 00:47:31,320
And what Jesus wants for them, he invites them to go take a break.

721
00:47:31,320 --> 00:47:37,020
He says, we're going to go to a desert place, to a desolate place, to a lonely place, and rest a while.

722
00:47:37,020 --> 00:47:40,840
That is what they wanted, and that is what Jesus wanted for them.

723
00:47:40,880 --> 00:47:42,620
So they set sail for a remote getaway.

724
00:47:42,620 --> 00:47:43,920
Anybody remembering this story?

725
00:47:43,920 --> 00:47:47,320
And when they arrive, they find what?

726
00:47:47,320 --> 00:47:51,600
A remote, desolate place for a nice, restful, relaxing time?

727
00:47:51,600 --> 00:47:53,600
Nope.

728
00:47:53,600 --> 00:47:57,960
They find a large crowd of people who are waiting there for them.

729
00:47:57,960 --> 00:48:01,500
And it says that Jesus saw them, and he had compassion on them,

730
00:48:01,500 --> 00:48:03,580
because they were like sheep without a shepherd.

731
00:48:05,880 --> 00:48:08,700
He sat there, and he taught them, and he encouraged them,

732
00:48:08,700 --> 00:48:12,560
and he invited them to participate in his kingdom for hours.

733
00:48:12,560 --> 00:48:17,360
And the disciples, in classic disciple fashion, are like, all right, enough with that.

734
00:48:17,360 --> 00:48:18,600
Can we send them home?

735
00:48:18,600 --> 00:48:19,660
Because they're all hungry.

736
00:48:19,660 --> 00:48:21,260
They're getting annoying.

737
00:48:21,260 --> 00:48:24,160
We're hangry.

738
00:48:24,160 --> 00:48:25,540
Can we just end this already?

739
00:48:25,920 --> 00:48:29,960
And in classic Jesus fashion, he says, you feed them.

740
00:48:29,960 --> 00:48:35,180
And then in classic discipleship, disciples fashion, they say, how?

741
00:48:35,180 --> 00:48:37,560
We have two fish and five little rolls.

742
00:48:37,560 --> 00:48:41,800
This is a classic Jesus disciple conversation.

743
00:48:41,800 --> 00:48:44,420
So Jesus does what only Jesus can do,

744
00:48:44,420 --> 00:48:47,860
and he multiplies what the disciples have until the entire crowd is fed,

745
00:48:47,860 --> 00:48:51,540
and there is more than enough food left over.

746
00:48:52,300 --> 00:48:56,460
This passage has a ton of implications, theologically and personally,

747
00:48:56,460 --> 00:49:00,240
but I think the reason that God keeps coming back to me with it is

748
00:49:00,240 --> 00:49:04,860
